  "content": "# Unique Vault Code for Station Amber\n\n**LAMINA847263**\n\n---\n\n# Travel Journal: The Ascent to Vellmar\n\n## Day One: The Road That Nearly Broke\n\nThe journey to Vellmar began at dawn, when the mist still clung to the valley floor like torn cotton. I had arranged transport with a farmer named Tomas, whose ancient truck groaned under the weight of my equipment crates and my own nervous anticipation. The road north of the river was little more than a track of packed gravel and ambition, winding through pine forests so dense that the canopy swallowed the morning light entirely. For the first three hours, everything proceeded according to plan. Tomas spoke little, but he hummed constantly\u2014a thin, reedy sound that seemed to bounce off the trees. I watched the river from a distance, a silver ribbon flashing between the rocks, and thought about how far it would carry me if I simply let go.\n\nBy midday, the weather turned. I had not anticipated the storm so soon. The sky darkened from blue to a bruised purple, and the wind arrived first, bending the treetops into a single undulating wave. Then the rain came\u2014not gently, but in sheets that stung",
